=== Atonement
--- Atonement & Reconciliation in Romans [title]
overline: Romans 5:11
heading: Atonement & Reconciliation in Romans

--- The Word “Atonement”
kicker: Atonement
stat: 70 | times in the KJV
stat: 69 | times in the Old Testament
stat: 1 | time in the New Testament
callout: 70 — God’s number of divine completion and perfection

--- Romans 5:11
kicker: Atonement
big: Romans 5:11 | mark: atonement
p: This “atonement” translates the Greek **katallagē (καταλλαγή)**, meaning **reconciliation** — the restoration of a broken relationship, bringing sinful humanity back into favor and peace with a holy God.
note: Modern translations miss the mark.

--- Key Verses
kicker: Atonement
big: Romans 5:10 | mark: reconciled
p: [[Romans 5:11]]: the atonement [**reconciliation**].
p: Atonement and Reconciliation are synonymous: **God’s purchase of the sins of the world by the blood of Christ**
p: This brings the offer of **peace with God** through the gift of **salvation** — a gift that must be **received by faith**.

